From 6b890a10bbcd2f1db14c613e917f940ed64be921 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:52:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cli): CLI exit cancels its in-flight background review;
 one-shots never fork one [daveey]

On 2026-10-29 20:16 PDT (MacBook, core cb1aa70f, session 20261029_201245_dfaf9b), a post-turn
review fork's first API call returned after CLI cleanup had run. Its skill_view call then failed
with "cannot schedule new futures after interpreter shutdown". The review runs on a daemon
bg-review thread. TUI session finalize cancels it (#102895) and serve retirement fences it, but the
classic CLI exit path did neither, so the process exited underneath a review that was still
dispatching tools. On hermes-hub, 142 of 142 platform=cli review forks between 10-29 23:01 and
10-30 03:40 UTC never completed. Each one only cost a full-history request.

- cli_shutdown._cancel_background_review_on_exit: the CLI session end owns the review. It runs
  the same bounded cancel the TUI uses, first in _run_cleanup (before resource teardown) and in
  _finalize_single_query (before memory shutdown).
- Single-query CLI agents (-q, kanban workers) and hermes -z are built with
  skip_background_review=True (cron precedent). The process exits right after the turn, so the
  review could never finish. Interactive CLI reviews are unchanged.

Test: tests/hermes_cli/test_cli_exit_cancels_background_review.py. A subprocess runs the real
_run_cleanup plus interpreter shutdown with a review in flight. Before the fix it fails with
TOOL_REFUSED "cannot schedule new futures after interpreter shutdown"; after the fix the review
is cancelled and dispatches no tool. Also tests that -q/-z pass skip_background_review and that
interactive mode keeps it.
